(---) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Executive Summary) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HealthApp is a healthcare management application built with Next.js, TypeScript, React, MongoDB,) Tj T*
(and custom JWT authentication. It supports patients, doctors, pharmacists, and administrators.) Tj T*
(The system processes sensitive healthcare information including medical records, prescriptions,) Tj T*
(allergies, blood groups, emergency contacts, and appointment information.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This assessment identified eight distinct non-payment security vulnerabilities in the original) Tj T*
(implementation. The findings cover broken access control, authentication bypass, weak) Tj T*
(cryptography, secret management, object-level authorization, sensitive-data exposure, credential) Tj T*
(disclosure, and security misconfiguration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Payment-related vulnerabilities are intentionally excluded from this report scope.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Technology and Security Scope) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Next.js App Router) Tj T*
(- TypeScript and React) Tj T*
(- MongoDB database) Tj T*
(- Custom JWT authentication using jose) Tj T*
(- HTTP-only authentication cookie) Tj T*
(- PBKDF2 password hashing) Tj T*
(- Role-based patient, doctor, pharmacist, and administrator workflows) Tj T*
(- API route handlers under app/api) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The assessment used white-box source inspection. Black-box confirmation using OWASP ZAP and) Tj T*
(regression tests should be added before final submission.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Vulnerability Summary) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ID    Vulnerability    Severity    OWASP category    ) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VULN-01    Privilege escalation during registration    Critical    A01 Broken Access Control    ) Tj T*
(VULN-02    Middleware authentication bypass    Critical    A07 Identification and Authentication) Tj T*
(Failures) Tj T*
(VULN-03    Weak password hashing    High    A02 Cryptographic Failures    ) Tj T*
(VULN-04    Hard-coded JWT secret fallback    Critical    A02 Cryptographic Failures    ) Tj T*
ET

endstream
