(VULN-05    Broken object-level authorization / IDOR    High    A01 Broken Access Control    ) Tj T*
(VULN-06    Excessive medical-data exposure    High    A01 Broken Access Control    ) Tj T*
(VULN-07    Password-hash disclosure    High    A02 Cryptographic Failures    ) Tj T*
(VULN-08    Security misconfiguration    Medium    A05 Security Misconfiguration    ) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Detailed Findings) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VULN-01: Privilege Escalation During Registration) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Severity: Critical) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Description: The public registration endpoint accepts the role value directly from the request.) Tj T*
(A user can register as an administrator, doctor, or pharmacist without administrator approval.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Evidence: app/api/auth/register/route.ts accepts role from the request body, stores it in the) Tj T*
(user document, and places it in the JWT.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Impact: An unauthenticated attacker can create a privileged account and access administrative or) Tj T*
(staff functionality.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recommended fix: Public registration must always create a patient account. Staff accounts should) Tj T*
(be created only through an authenticated administrator workflow or invitation process. The) Tj T*
(server must use an allowlist and must never trust a client-provided privileged role.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Verification evidence: Attempt registration with role: "admin"; the secure version should reject) Tj T*
(the request or create only a patient account.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VULN-02: Middleware Authentication Bypass) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Severity: Critical) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Description: The middleware identifies public paths using pathname.startsWith\(path\). Since / is) Tj T*
(included in publicPaths, every pathname starts with /. As a result, protected page routes can) Tj T*
(bypass middleware authentication.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Evidence: middleware.ts defines const publicPaths = ["/auth/login", "/auth/register", "/"] and) Tj T*
(checks pathname.startsWith\(path\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Impact: Unauthenticated users may directly access protected application pages. API routes still) Tj T*
(require their own checks, but the page-level security boundary is ineffective.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recommended fix: Match exact public routes or use a safe route predicate. For example, compare) Tj T*
(pathname === "/" instead of using startsWith for the root route. Add middleware tests for) Tj T*
(anonymous access to every protected role area.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Verification evidence: Request /admin/dashboard, /doctor/dashboard, and /patient/dashboard) Tj T*
(without a cookie. The secure version should redirect to login.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VULN-03: Weak Password Hashing) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET

endstream
