(Severity: Medium) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Description: The application does not visibly configure important HTTP security headers, and the) Tj T*
(Next.js configuration ignores TypeScript and ESLint errors during builds.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Evidence: next.config.mjs disables build failure for TypeScript and ESLint errors. No) Tj T*
(application-wide CSP, HSTS, frame protection, MIME-sniffing protection, or Referrer-Policy) Tj T*
(configuration was identified.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Impact: Missing headers increase exposure to clickjacking, MIME confusion, information leakage,) Tj T*
(and script-injection impact. Ignoring build errors can allow security defects to reach) Tj T*
(deployment.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recommended fix: Configure security headers in middleware or Next.js headers configuration.) Tj T*
(Enable TypeScript and lint failures in CI and production builds. Add automated checks for) Tj T*
(required headers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Verification evidence: Inspect response headers with OWASP ZAP or browser developer tools and) Tj T*
(confirm required headers are present in the secure version.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Additional Security Observations) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The following issues should be assessed and may be included as additional findings after) Tj T*
(testing:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- JWTs remain valid for seven days after logout because there is no revocation or token-version) Tj T*
(mechanism.) Tj T*
(- QR codes contain patient identifiers and have no expiry, signature, nonce, or revocation) Tj T*
(mechanism.) Tj T*
(- Password-change verification uses bcrypt while login uses PBKDF2, causing password changes to) Tj T*
(fail for normal PBKDF2 users.) Tj T*
(- State-changing cookie-authenticated APIs do not show explicit CSRF tokens or origin) Tj T*
(validation.) Tj T*
(- Several API routes perform minimal validation and have no visible rate limiting, pagination,) Tj T*
(or request-size policy.) Tj T*
(- Dependency vulnerabilities must be confirmed with pnpm audit before being reported as CVEs.) Tj T*
(- SQL injection is not applicable because the application uses MongoDB. XSS and NoSQL injection) Tj T*
(require black-box confirmation before being claimed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Recommended Testing Plan) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Create a baseline copy or Git tag of the original vulnerable implementation.) Tj T*
(2. Add one security regression test for each vulnerability.) Tj T*
(3. Use OWASP ZAP against a local test deployment.) Tj T*
(4. Test anonymous access to protected pages.) Tj T*
(5. Test role tampering during registration.) Tj T*
(6. Test cross-patient medical-record requests.) Tj T*
(7. Test sensitive-field leakage from admin endpoints.) Tj T*
(8. Inspect security response headers.) Tj T*
(9. Run pnpm audit and record the result separately from source-code findings.) Tj T*
ET

endstream
