() Tj T*
(7. Secure Software Engineering Practices) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(These vulnerabilities could have been prevented through:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Server-side allowlists for roles and permissions.) Tj T*
(- Centralized authorization middleware and resource ownership checks.) Tj T*
(- Secure secret validation during startup.) Tj T*
(- Modern password hashing standards.) Tj T*
(- Schema validation for every API payload.) Tj T*
(- Data-minimizing response DTOs.) Tj T*
(- Threat modeling for healthcare data and QR workflows.) Tj T*
(- Security-focused code review and pull-request checks.) Tj T*
(- Dependency scanning and lockfile maintenance.) Tj T*
(- Automated security regression tests and OWASP ZAP scans in CI.) Tj T*
(- Fail-closed production builds that do not ignore type or lint errors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. Limitations) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This initial report is based on source-code inspection. Database indexes, production deployment) Tj T*
(headers, environment variables, live MongoDB permissions, and runtime behavior were not) Tj T*
(independently verified. The final submission should clearly label black-box findings, white-box) Tj T*
(findings, and assumptions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
